    "notes": "Reviewed source mapping. Basis: AB 325 (Stats. 2025, ch. 338) adds Cal. Bus. & Prof. Code § 16729(a)-(b) (common pricing algorithm used or distributed as part of an antitrust conspiracy, or with coercion) and § 16756.1 (Cartwright Act pleading standard). SB 763 (Stats. 2025, ch. 426) amends § 16755 (higher fines) and adds § 16755.1 (civil penalty up to $1,000,000) and § 16762 (cumulative remedies). All six rules are marked in_force with a 2026-01-01 effective date. That date is derived from the chaptered metadata (approved Oct. 6, 2025, majority vote, no urgency clause) plus the Secretary of State's general rule that regular-session statutes take effect Jan. 1 of the following year. These are general antitrust provisions, not a categorical ban on rental software. § 16729 reaches rental pricing only where its conditions are met. Unknown coverage addresses: 250. ",
